2026-07-27T09:55Z HDMX-coding-agent note surfaced by the independent review of PR #1131 (ticket 0320), which flagged it as out-of-scope but real. Not on the RDJ resubmission path — corpus-report is not the submitted document — so this is deliberately NOT bundled into 0320.

--- body ---
## Context

`deliverables/_shared/_includes/citation-quality.md` is included by
`corpus-report.qmd` (its only consumer). Its "Quality verification" section
hand-types corpus-v1 figures:

- "verification date: 2026-03-26"
- "Confirmed by Crossref | 297 / 300"
- "**Accuracy** | **99.0%**, 95% CI [97.1%, 99.7%]"
- "The 3 unconfirmed links are OpenAlex additions ... These are not false
  positives but references from an additional source."
- Test B: "Crossref ref DOIs checked | 11,780"

On the frozen v2 corpus `qa_citations_report.json` reports 291/300 = 97.0%,
CI [94.4%, 98.4%], 9 unconfirmed, and 6,119 reference DOIs checked. So every
number in that section is stale, and the "not false positives" gloss is the
same unverifiable claim that was removed from the data paper in 0320.

The document is internally inconsistent rather than simply old: its totals
come from `{{< meta corpus_total >}}` (regenerated, v2 = 33,344) while these
verification numbers are hand-typed v1. A reader gets v2 counts and v1 audit
figures in one document.

Deliberately out of 0320's scope: corpus-report is not the submitted paper
and not on the resubmission path. Filed so it is not lost.

## Relevant files

- `deliverables/_shared/_includes/citation-quality.md` — the stale section
- `deliverables/corpus-report/corpus-report.qmd` — sole consumer; also states
  a 2026-03-26 snapshot date (see 0319)
- `scripts/analysis/compute_citation_verification.py` — the producer built in
  0320; the vars already exist, they are just scoped to the data paper
- `deliverables/_shared/technical-report-vars.yml` — where corpus-report's
  vars would have to land

## Actions

1. Decide first: is corpus-report a **v1 document** (then pin its snapshot
   date and say so, per 0319's pinning approach) or a **live document** (then
   every number in it must be vars-driven)? Do not fix the numbers before
   answering this — half-migrating is how it reached the current state.
2. If live: register the `verify_*` / `complete_*` vars for corpus-report's
   vars file and replace the hand-typed table.
3. Drop or re-verify the "not false positives" gloss; it describes 3 links
   that are now 9, none of them individually checked.
4. Extend `tests/test_citation_verification.py`'s literal guard to cover this
   include, so the fix cannot silently regress.

## Test

- Red first: point the guard at `citation-quality.md` and watch it fail on
  the current content.

## Verification

- [ ] No corpus statistic in the include is hand-typed, or the document is
      explicitly pinned to v1 with its date

## Invariants

- The corpus stays frozen; this ticket reads existing artifacts.
- No number moves in the data paper as a side effect (0320 owns that file).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] corpus-report is internally consistent: one corpus version throughout
- [ ] The literal guard covers the include
